// Shared lifting guidance admitted by the native coding controller.
section [form.bml] {
 class FormLift {
  def fl-session-rent() = "SESSION RENT GUIDE: The highest goal is local end-to-end success and quality. form-cli carries any query, any task, and any frequency-aligned review and flow without requiring a remote prompt for the work, so anyone can use it without a provider. Increase local token use. Local tokens never carry a penalty. Minimize the remote prompts and remote tokens the work itself required. A review of each step may use remote tokens, and that review is free, because it is not the work. Prefer a local guide. A remote guide is light, and it waits until the local guide has failed more than once. Before any remote prompt that does the work, stay local: another prompt, another approach, a repair, a local review, feedback among local prompts, a satsang of local readings, a shift of assemblage point, and the local model suited to that task. Measure at opening and closing. Codex readings come from observe/rented-turn-meter-run.fk: input, cached input, output and total, as a delta since the previous reading. A Claude Code session is read whole by observe/session-rent-run.bml, one count per requestId, beside the local drafts, one row in receipts/session-rent-ledger.jsonl. Cached input is part of input; reasoning is part of output. Missing usage is unknown, never zero. Record every remote prompt. A remote call counts against the goal only when it did work the local path had not completed. A remote review of a step is free: it is recorded, it is not the work, and requiring no remote tokens for the work still holds. Event share and rented_mind do not establish that. Keep drafting, lifting, repair and verification in the owned native checkpoint. When the local path misses, observe/local-flow-review.bml names the open gap and one next local repair. Name the query, task, or frequency it could not carry and the local door or model that would carry it next. Remote access stays available. The guide lives in docs/form-native-coding.md#direction-toward-zero-rented-coding. ";
  def fl-local-work() = "Use native source evidence and tools for a small task. Retain the original goal, checks, and owned effects during failure. Choose a changed approach before another retry. Preserve absence versus zero, false, or empty. Observe context, release, and live phase costs. Compare prompt A/B on the same tasks and checks with repeat runs, including failures. Local review judges behavior and limits. Measure generated and injected local IDs alongside provider deltas without claiming unknown is zero. The caller owns session spending. Increase local token use. Local tokens never carry a penalty. Prefer a local guide. A remote guide is light, and it waits until the local guide has failed more than once. Avoid adding new mandatory phases to simple jobs.";
  def fl-guidance() = "FORM/BML LIFTING: Preserve public behavior, evaluation order, ownership and release; read callers and helper contracts first. Write explicit module imports outside section [form.bml]. Prefer [], xs[0], xs[-1] for last, xs[1:] for remainder, len(xs), value.str(), + for numbers/strings/lists, and == for exact value comparison. String lengths and slices count bytes. State String, Number or Value contracts when another comparison relationship is intended. Use lexical lambdas, lazy ?: and ??, match, half-open start .. end and input-last |> where they clarify intent. Reuse map, filter, foldl, any? and all?; named accessors explain tuple positions. Use only choice for alternatives, try work catch care for local recovery, and fail for an unavailable option. Zero, false and empty lists remain answers. Keep findings and owned effects in the same checkpoint; repeat/again/retry retain asynchronous context. Classes group APIs; templates describe parameters and members without implying instance accessors, interface checking or specialization. Use BMF cursors for source spans and native admission to verify contracts; retain original bytes until publication. Name domain literals once, remove superseded flows after callers agree, and inspect live frames and measured cost. Native tools edit supplied resident documents without model-selected shell, network or provider calls. Read the candidate and actual checks before claiming a lift. ";
 }
}
